{
  "concept": "The sum u + v and the difference u - v are the two diagonals of the same parallelogram, because subtracting v is the same as adding the reversed vector -v head-to-tail with u.",
  "figureType": "diagram",
  "elements": [
    "Left parallelogram: dark navy outline, lower-left vertex as common origin, bottom edge horizontal, right edge slanting up-right",
    "Left parallelogram both diagonals drawn as thin navy lines (lower-left to upper-right, and upper-left to lower-right)",
    "Left: bottom edge with orange arrowhead pointing right, italic label u below it",
    "Left: right slanted edge with orange arrowhead pointing up-and-right, italic label v to its right",
    "Left: main diagonal from lower-left to upper-right ending in orange arrowhead, italic label u + v placed above the diagonal near its midpoint",
    "Right parallelogram: identical navy outline and thin diagonals, placed beside the left one",
    "Right: top edge with orange arrowhead pointing right, italic label u above it",
    "Right: bottom edge also labeled italic u (no arrowhead emphasis or a faint one) to show the translated copy",
    "Right: slanted right edge with orange arrowhead pointing down-and-right, italic label -v to its right",
    "Right: diagonal descending from upper-left vertex toward lower-right vertex, labeled italic u - v near its midpoint",
    "Vertex dots at the four corners of each parallelogram",
    "Optional legend/caption strip: 'addition = long diagonal from the common tail' vs 'subtraction = diagonal joining the two heads'",
    "Ghosted (dashed grey) copy of v shown when -v is displayed, to mark the reversal"
  ],
  "interactions": [
    {
      "id": "operation",
      "type": "toggle",
      "teaches": "Subtraction is not a new operation: flipping v to -v turns the same parallelogram's other diagonal into the answer.",
      "label": "Operation",
      "options": ["u + v", "u - v", "Show both"],
      "default": "u + v"
    },
    {
      "id": "construction",
      "type": "button",
      "teaches": "The resultant is the endpoint of a deliberate head-to-tail construction, not an arbitrary line inside the shape.",
      "label": "Construction step",
      "states": ["draw u", "attach v (or -v) head-to-tail", "complete parallelogram", "reveal resultant diagonal"],
      "default": "draw u"
    },
    {
      "id": "selectDiagonal",
      "type": "click",
      "teaches": "Each diagonal belongs to a specific pair of side vectors — clicking one lights up exactly the two edges that generate it.",
      "teaches_note": "click a diagonal to highlight it and its two component edges"
    }
  ],
  "demo_steps": [
    {
      "title": "Start with u alone",
      "narration": "Only the vector u is drawn from the common tail, pointing right along the bottom edge. Everything else in the parallelogram will be built from here.",
      "state": { "operation": "u + v", "construction": "draw u" }
    },
    {
      "title": "Attach v head-to-tail",
      "narration": "v is placed with its tail at the head of u, slanting up and to the right. The free end of v is already the answer to u + v.",
      "state": { "operation": "u + v", "construction": "attach v (or -v) head-to-tail" }
    },
    {
      "title": "Close the parallelogram",
      "narration": "Copies of u and v complete the figure, showing that the head-to-tail path and the parallelogram give the same endpoint.",
      "state": { "operation": "u + v", "construction": "complete parallelogram" }
    },
    {
      "title": "Reveal u + v",
      "narration": "The diagonal from the shared tail to the opposite corner is u + v — the long diagonal of the parallelogram.",
      "state": { "operation": "u + v", "construction": "reveal resultant diagonal" }
    },
    {
      "title": "Flip v into -v",
      "narration": "Switching to subtraction reverses v: the orange arrow on the slanted edge now points down and to the right, with the original v ghosted behind it.",
      "state": { "operation": "u - v", "construction": "attach v (or -v) head-to-tail" }
    },
    {
      "title": "Reveal u - v",
      "narration": "Adding -v head-to-tail to u lands on the other corner, so u - v is the second diagonal, running from the head of v down to the head of u.",
      "state": { "operation": "u - v", "construction": "reveal resultant diagonal" }
    },
    {
      "title": "Both diagonals at once",
      "narration": "Displayed together, the sum and the difference are simply the two diagonals of one parallelogram. Click either diagonal to highlight the pair of edges that produce it.",
      "state": { "operation": "Show both", "construction": "reveal resultant diagonal" }
    }
  ],
  "keyInsight": "One parallelogram holds both answers: its long diagonal from the common tail is u + v, and the diagonal joining the two heads is u - v, because u - v is just u + (-v).",
  "reconstructionNotes": "Two congruent slanted parallelograms side by side on white, each outlined in thick dark navy (#1F4E79) with thin navy diagonals inside. Bottom edges horizontal; right edges slant up-right at roughly 60°. Active vectors are drawn as bold orange (#E8622A) segments with solid arrowheads laid on top of the navy edges; inactive edges stay plain navy. Left figure: orange arrow right along the bottom edge labeled italic u, orange arrow up-right along the right edge labeled italic v, and an orange-tipped diagonal from the lower-left vertex to the upper-right vertex labeled italic u + v just above its midpoint. Right figure: orange arrow right along the top edge labeled italic u above it, the bottom edge also labeled italic u, an orange arrow pointing down-right on the right edge labeled italic -v, and the descending diagonal from the upper-left vertex toward the lower-right vertex labeled italic u - v near its midpoint. When -v is shown, render the original v as a dashed grey arrow to mark the reversal. Labels in serif italic, matching textbook style. Highlight state: selected diagonal thickens and turns amber with a soft glow, its two component edges also turn amber, all other strokes fade to light grey."
}

